Indeed. The most reasonably practical approache I've seen to
roleplaying nethack is not unlike: The contents of the Guidebook and
the information available via commands like '?' and '/' are considered
to be your character's general world-knowledge, obtained prior to
entering the mines.

This, together with ordinary prudence, can get you quite far. (It's still
very hard, both in terms of game difficulty and in the discipline required
for a fully-spoiled player to avoid using "unearned" knowledge. Dismissed
as Not My Cup of Tea, Thank You after a couple attempts.)


